        "text": {
            "description_html": "<b>AHI SIG141, Stainless Steel Deco Door Lever</b>\r\n\r\n<p>\r\nThis AHI made Stainless Steel Deco Leverset is basic enough to effortlessly add just the right amount of retro detailing to your rooms; and also because its design is so simple, this lever is capable of beautifully integrating into whatever furnishing you have without having to overhaul your entire décor. Easy to install, it will fit standard door preparations. Made out of 304 stainless steel, the Deco Lever is available in passage, privacy, and dummy functions. This solid stainless steel leverset can be used in any commercial or residential setting where durability and style are desired. The Deco Stainless Steel Leverset is ADA compliant. It comes in satin stainless steel finish. This lever and rose set can be adjusted for 1-3/8 inch to 2 inch thick doors with 2-3/8 inch or 2-3/4 inch backsets.\r\n</p>\r\n\r\n<p>\r\n<img src=\"https://cdn.shopify.com/s/files/1/0766/1489/3857/files/AHI-SIG141-Specifications.gif?v=1704354719\" width=\"391\" height=\"215\" border=\"0\" alt=\"AHI SIG141 Deco Lever Specifications\">\r\n</p>\r\n\r\n<p>\r\n<b>Features</b> of the AHI SIG141 Stainless Steel Deco Leverset:\r\n<ul>\r\n<li>For residential or commercial applications</li>\r\n<li>Fits standard door cut outs (2-1/8\" pre-drilled doors)</li>\r\n<li>Field reversible tubular latch</li>\r\n<li>Premium latch requires only 28° rotation to retract latchbolt</li>\r\n<li>Meets standards of the <a href=\"/pages/ada-compliant\">Americans with Disabilities Act (ADA)</a></li>\r\n</ul>\r\n\r\n</p>\r\n\r\n<p>\r\n<b>Specifications</b> of the SIG141 Stainless Steel Deco Lever:\r\n<ul>\r\n<li>Material: 304 Stainless Steel</li>\r\n<li>Finish: <b>Satin Stainless Steel</b></li>\r\n<li>Lever Length: 5.16\" (129 mm)</li>\r\n<li>Lever Projection: 2\" (50 mm)</li>\r\n<li>Spindle Width: 0.31\" (8 mm)</li>\r\n<li>Rose Diameter: 2.52\" (64 mm)</li>\r\n<li>Door Thickness: adjustable for 1-3/8\" to 2\"</li>\r\n<li>Backset: 2-3/8\" or 2-3/4\"</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n</p>\r\n\r\n<p>\r\n<b>When Selecting a Function:</b>\r\n<ul>\r\n<li><b>Single Dummy:</b> For use as a door pull or to match trim. Trim is on one side of door. Lever is surface mounted (mounting plate screws to the doors face).</li>\r\n<li><b>Double Dummy:</b> No door latch. Door levers on both sides of the door. For use with a standard 2-1/8\" bore hole pre-drilled door. </li>\r\n<li><b>Passage (hall or closet):</b> For doors that don't need locking. Latch operates from either side of door.</li>\r\n<li><b>Privacy (bedroom or bathroom):</b> For doors that could need privacy locking. Latch operates from either side. Push button on interior rose engages\r\n privacy; emergency release hole is on exterior rose. Turning inside lever will release privacy push button and retract the door latch.</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n</p>\r\n\r\n<p>\r\n<b>Note: Single Dummy is Handed</b>. All other functions are non-handed. <a href=\"/pages/how-to-order-door-hardware\"><b>Handing Guide</b></a>\r\n</p>",
